            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a331"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts25" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts31">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I think definitely as an adult, I think that I wanted to have the bond we have now my whole life, but it was so hard when I was a kid because I was so lost and I was so confused. And it was hard to know you were on my side. That's something you used to say to me all the time when I was a kid: I'm on your side, I'm on your side, but I never heard you. You'd always remind me of your love for me, but I never understood it. I used to say, like, you hate me, you hate me. Saw so clearly as an adult what I couldn't see as a kid, and that is that you love me so deeply and wholeheartedly. My happiness was at the top of your priority list. Even if that meant you not making always the best decisions, you were trying. And so it allowed me to trust you and just feel like I could be fully open, fully vulnerable with you. And it just made me feel like very, really safe with you.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
