        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a334"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts117" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts125">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>I understand and relate to the childhood talk because even for me, like it's hard to talk about some of the darkest times of my childhood because I know that you feel guilt just like I feel guilt. And so if I'm just fully telling you, how much it hurt me the things you did, of course that's gonna weigh on you. Just like you tell me like you know, how hard it was and, you know, being a mom to me, it was like a burden sometimes. Like those things are gonna, you know, they they hurt the other person, but it's important to express them, but maybe just not to each other, like maybe in therapy and</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a395"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts128" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts129">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a396"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts130" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts131">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a335"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts143" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts145">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>That's a hard one. What's something I feel like you don't fully understand about me?</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a336"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts147" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts149">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Sometimes maybe the way my mind thinks, um</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a337"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts151" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts161">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>How I see the world, I do think we're very similar, like in how we see the world, but we live in really different spaces in the world, you know? Like I'm around so many different types of people, you know, the way I grew up, how curious I was about the world, how I literally have friends from, you know, every different continent, every different racial background, you know, friends from every different sector of the LGBTQ plus community. I have friends from every different religion, you know, and so I get this really cool experience of talking to all these people. And I know you love coming around my friends because like yesterday too, like you get to have these really deep conversations because you have such a open and inquisitive mind, which that's one of the things I love so much about you, especially for being a white woman of your age, you know, with the financial status that you're in. But I think because you are so interested in the world and humanity and you are always paying attention through news outlets, et cetera, I have a different experience because I don't listen to the news. I talk to people. So sometimes it's hard to, like, even though you are so open to understanding, we live in like two different worlds in that aspect because, you know, you, different generations, yeah. But I love that we talk about it all the time. And, you know, we've really gotten to a place where I feel like we have a lot of respect for each other when talking about those things, or it wasn't always like that, because I would just get angry or upset, or you know, you don't fully understand this. But you've also become so open-minded, too. So yeah, I think that's the only thing I can really think of. I feel like besides that, you understand me very well, even in the areas that we are different.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a398"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts164" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts165">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a399"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts166" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts167">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Absolutely.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a338"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts173" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts183">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah, I think I think it's hard for me to understand too. Like, I think when I was younger, obviously I was so misunderstood. And that was one of the darkest times of my life, fourth grade. I mean, I was being bullied brutally. Yeah, I know. I was being bullied so brutally. And um I was so misunderstood and I think the people I met at the time who it just so happened to be black especially, I mean she impacted my life on a whole new level. Then she brought me around her family and her friends and her community, and I was just completely engulfed in love and support, and I felt so seen. And people that looked like me never saw me. I feel like I've always related to other people. Because I was other than [unclear] so much, yeah.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
        <ANNOTATION>
            <ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION ANNOTATION_ID="a339"
                TIME_SLOT_REF1="ts184" TIME_SLOT_REF2="ts192">
                <ANNOTATION_VALUE>Yeah. You were skinny, you were popular, you were a hippie girl with long hair. You were white. You were tan.</ANNOTATION_VALUE>
            </ALIGNABLE_ANNOTATION>
        </ANNOTATION>
